hello and welcome to Playstation grenade  for tonight is one of the most content  filled games I have ever played  it's like minecraft mixed with wave and  tower defense and a crazy level of  micromanagement and detail many of the  skills you will pick up through osmosis  but there's a few things that slip under  the net after 20 hours of play I've  barely scratched the surface of this  beast but even in that short amount of  time I found 10 things I wish I knew one  had first started I'm starting with  something which is counterintuitive to  most gamers on most levels you are given  a task to complete such as finding and  activating an Atlas don't rush to it  leave it as long as you can the game  world rewards you for scavenging looting  and exploring so run into the wilderness  and find activities to complete rescuing  survivors thanks again for your house  see you soon  find blueprints to help you craft  buildings which don't look like basic  cube structures completing these will  reward you handsomely by simply  following the design you can build some  really impressive structures this is the  beat yard there are little minigames  defined to and boosters to unlock once  these are complete now's the time to go  to the original task in the world  so remember explore the world you are  thrown into you may find a treasure  chest r2 or something which can be  searched by the way don't destroy  something before you search it or all  that precious loot is gone for good the  stumbling block we all run into quite  early on in the game is locating ammo  resources our integral part of the game  and nuts and bolts are the resource  you're probably running low on they can  be found in many places but the most  reliable way to farm them is by smashing  the stout of the vehicles you see I  suggest going to the towns if you need  to craft ammo as vehicles are few and  far between in the countryside later in  the game a mission named repair the  shelter will ask you to search for these  transparent objects the majority of  these badboys contain up to 400 nuts and  bolts so farm to your heart's content  your first real mission will see you  building a storm shield home base you'll  be coming back here regularly and  whatever you build will stay here  indefinitely so plan what you build and  don't make a huge embarrassing mess like  me if you change your mind later on and  tear everything down it will be  massively time-consuming and it won't  yield many materials in return and as  the game progresses the quality of your  structures the traps you create are  imperative to survival  so always plan what you want to build  speaking of traps if you look closely  enough you will see your backpack has a  limit to the amount of items it can  carry a great way to make space in your  rucksack is to craft numerous traps this  will also keep you one step ahead when  it's time to build defenses just be  mindful of the materials it takes to  craft those  level of your character trying not to  play as one single character as each of  them has benefits and a few limits to  the ninjas double-jump is very useful  when exploring what other characters  have constructing ability and in the  later levels these are essential to  maintaining your structures so my advice  try out a few characters and switch  things up every now and again remember  to level your characters too and improve  their stats and abilities  this goes for weapons too and pretty  much everything else in this game level  it up level of your favorite guns to  improve them constantly eventually each  gun will break but don't worry too much  when you craft another it will retain  the level you progressed it - so don't  save it for a rainy day use it and craft  another one that time is right another  tip I wish I knew early on was the  recycle function when weapons are close  to breaking you can opt to recycle them  the benefit to doing this are the  resources you receive in return you  won't get enough back to craft the same  gun again but you will receive materials  which may be difficult to find in the  open world so recycle to your heart's  content oh and by the way the guns you  crap yourself will have far superior  stats and perks to those you find in the  game world so when you get a new gun  schematic craft it and try it out  furthermore as you level up your skill  tree recycle old weapon schematics - and  other low level stuff you don't really  want such as survivor cards retire them  to make room for higher-level survivors  as well as gain a little xp to the next  tip isn't accessible from the beginning  but once you start to upgrade your skill  tree it will be before each level during  the character lobby screen select your  character and add gadgets to your  loadout I only have two at this point  the first is a health boost to your  character and other allies that may be  in the vicinity and my current favorite  gadget is a freaking airstrike both are  perfect for difficult sections in  calculus  finally building a defense the Cossacks  will take the path of least resistance  trying to get to whatever you're  defending so keep that in mind when  you're creating a mace for them to run  through if you build a fan area too  extensively the enemy will simply ignore  it and your hard work is ruined  give the hook a line to run through  known as funneling then sit back and  watch the carnage  so that's it that's ten super quick tips  when you're trying to get your head  around fortnight and guess what that's  only the beginning  take Florence cabbage before committing  to the task at hand farm  a most BOTS operate absolutely  everything recycle where possible use  your gadgets as soon as you can and plan  your defences accordingly there are so  many more areas to look at in fortnight  and if it's become useful I'll be sure  to create a new video for intermediate  players I need to take a minute to thank  youtuber and twitch streamers hack  office for helping me out on this one  he's in my suggested channels list so  please check him out if you want to see  some fortnight live and he pretty much  plays anything he can get his hands on -  I imagine from PlayStation grenade it's  been an absolute pleasure I'll see you  next time
 

